---
import NovaLayout from "../../layouts/NovaLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<NovaLayout title="About" description="David Eti builds infrastructure, breaks it on purpose and writes down what happened. Looking for sysadmin, infrastructure and DevOps roles in Belgium and the Netherlands." current="about">
  <section class="hero2"><div class="wrap prose-narrow">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1>I'm David Eti. I build infrastructure, break it on purpose, and write down what happened.</h1>
    <p class="lead">I'm a systems and infrastructure engineer in Belgium. I'm looking for sysadmin, infrastructure and DevOps roles in Belgium and the Netherlands, and I'm available now.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="nv-btn primary" href={base + "David_Eti_Systems_Infrastructure_CV.pdf"}>Download CV</a>
      <a class="nv-btn secondary" href="mailto:etidavid26@gmail.com">Email</a>
      <a class="nv-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/eti-david">LinkedIn ↗</a>
      <a class="nv-link" href="https://github.com/EtiDavid/Nova-Corp">GitHub ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec"><div class="wrap prose-narrow">
    <h2>What I built</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:8px">Nova Corp is a small fictional company with a real lab behind it, and I built all of it: Proxmox running inside VMware Workstation, a pfSense firewall with five VLANs, Windows Server 2025 with two domain controllers, Group Policy, file services with DFS, and PowerShell scripts for account work. <a href={base + "map/"}>The map</a> shows how the pieces connect.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:32px">How I work</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:8px">I write down what I expect before I test. I change one thing at a time. When something breaks, I separate the possible causes with a test before I touch anything: <a href={base + "incidents/dns-client-outage/"}>the DNS case</a> shows that best. When I can't prove a cause, I say so, as in <a href={base + "incidents/dc02-cannot-reach-dc01/"}>the CR-004 case</a>.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:32px">What Nova Corp doesn't cover</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:8px">It's a home lab, not an employer's network. It shows Windows Server, Active Directory, pfSense, virtualization, PowerShell, recovery and fault-finding. My Azure, Terraform and GitHub Actions work is in separate projects, such as <a href="https://github.com/EtiDavid/novapredict-devops-case-study">NovaPredict ↗</a>.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:32px">Languages</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:8px">English: fluent. Dutch: basic, and I'm studying for NT2.</p>
  </div></section>
</NovaLayout>
